{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>And you shall be holy, for I am holy.</b> Therefore I said to you: do not defile yourselves. The vav is like a weak pe, in the language of Ishmael. So too ויעזוב את עבדיו, and many like it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites the Arabic phonetic distinction between vav and weak pe (f) to explain the interchangeability he observes in certain Hebrew forms; the exact phonological argument is compressed and left as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:39.257449978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}